{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0182"},"reason":"a0182 body: Morpheus \"son of Hypnos\" → \"son of Somnus (the Greek Hypnos)\" (Ovid); Sertürner \"in December 1804 … first called it Morphium\" → \"in 1804 … called it principium somniferum and then named it Morphium after Morpheus\"; \"pharmacist\" → \"pharmacist's assistant\" — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Sert%C3%BCrner","by":"enrich batch 109","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a2422-a0386.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Sert%C3%BCrner"}]},
