{"seq":6,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0182"},"reason":"Proofread (reasons in the entries above / the batch report).","by":"enrich batch 109","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a2422-a0386.md","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",756],["-","Hypnos,"],["+","Somnus,"],["=",7],["-","sleep,"],["+","sleep"],["=",1],["+","(the Greek Hypnos), "],["=",28],["-","pharmacist"],["+","pharmacist's"],["=",1],["+","assistant "],["=",18],["-","December "],["=",4],["-","first "],["=",4],["+","principium somniferum, the “sleep-making principle”, and then named it "],["=",2],["+","after Morpheus "],["=",208],["-","“hermetic” from Hermes, "],["=",34],["+","Even “hermetic” has a divine pedigree: Hermes Trismegistus, “thrice-great Hermes” – the Greek god merged with the Egyptian Thoth – was revered as the founder of alchemy and credited with a secret way of sealing glass vessels, so a container closed airtight is hermetic, a sense recorded in English from about 1600. "],["=",27]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",750],["-","Hypnos"],["+","Somnus"],["=",1],["+","(griechisch Hypnos) "],["=",26],["-","Apotheker"],["+","Apothekergehilfe"],["=",5],["-","im Dezember "],["=",20],["+","principium somniferum, „schlafmachendes Prinzip“, und benannte es dann "],["=",14],["-","zunächst"],["+","nach"],["=",1],["+","Morpheus "],["=",192],["-","„hermetisch“ von Hermes, "],["=",32],["+","Selbst „hermetisch“ hat eine göttliche Herkunft: Hermes Trismegistos, der „dreimal größte Hermes“ – der griechische Gott, verschmolzen mit dem ägyptischen Thot –, galt als Begründer der Alchemie und Erfinder eines geheimen Verschlusses für Glasgefäße; deshalb heißt ein luftdicht verschlossener Behälter hermetisch, im Englischen seit etwa 1600 belegt. "],["=",25]]}],"hash":"31ab10e142fa"},
